Statistics Wizard [described]
A Chart, which you insert into a Frame, shows the Statistics Wizard.
Remarks
Select the command Statistics Wizard on the context menu of the Frame to open it.
Select the class(es) of object(s) for which you would like to show statistics values in the Chart. The Chart
only adds material flow objects to the display for which you selected the check box Resource Statistics on
the Tab Statistics.
Note
If you are working with a model that was created in a previous version of Plant Simulation that still
uses the outdated object names of these versions, the dialog shows a + sign in front of the new object
names.
• To inherit the settings you select below, select Inherit Settings 
 .
• Select the object classes in the group box Class for which you want to show statistics values in the
Chart. The Chart only adds material flow objects to the display for which you selected the check box
Resource Statistics on the Tab Statistics. You can select any number of classes.
Select the type of resource(s) for which you would like to show statistical data of the selected object(s)
in the Chart under Resource Type on the tab Statistics of an object collecting statistical data. With the
check boxes in the Statistics Wizard you can restrict, which objects Plant Simulation shows.
◦ Production is the default for the Source, Drain, Station, ParallelStation, AssemblyStation, and
DismantleStation.
Statistics Wizard [described]
11-4644 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

◦ Transport is the default for the PlaceBuffer, Buffer, Sorter, Track, TwoLaneTrack, Conveyor,
AngularConverter, Turntable, Transporter, and Container.
◦ Storage is the default for the Store.
• Select the criteria according to which Plant Simulation sorts statistical data from the drop-down list Sort
Criterion:
To sort the stations by their name in alphabetical order from A to Z, select Sort Criterion > Name.
To sort the stations in the order that meets your needs, drag the stations onto the Chart in the order it is
to show them.
To change the order at a later point in time, edit the table of the Input channels by cutting the respective
columns of the objects and pasting them in the desired order.
• Select the statistics type: Resource Statistics, Energy Statistics, or Occupancy.
• To also show statistical data of objects contained in Frames contained in the Frame in which the Chart is
located, select Include Subframes 
 .
• To reapply the settings while the simulation model is initialized, select Reapply at Init 
 .
• Click OK to display the Chart window with the settings you selected.
• If you drag a material flow object onto a Chart, which you have not configured yet, you have to select
the statistics type. By default, you can select Resource or Occupancy. If you activate energy features,
you can also select Energy. The different statistics types provide different value sets. The meaning of the
different states is described in the Statistics Report under Resource Statistics of Stationary Resources
and Energy Statistics — Energy Statistics.
• For the Statistics type > Resource, the Chart shows the Name of the object and the states it is in:
Working, Setting-Up, Waiting, Blocked, Powering up/down, Failed, Stopped, Paused, or Unplanned.
Statistics Wizard [described]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4645
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• For the Statistics Type > Energy, the Chart shows the energy states of the object:
Working, Setting-up, Operational, Failed, Standby, and Off.
Note
The energy states of the material flow objects differ from the resource states with the same name.
The values for the resource states refer to the statistics collection period, while the values for the
energy states refer to the total energy consumption.
• For the Statistics Type > Occupancy, the Chart shows the Name of the object and the number of parts
located on it. The colored bars serve for differentiating between the objects.
Statistics Wizard [described]
11-4646 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• You can also show the diagram picture of a Chart in an HtmlReport, compare Display a Chart.
Statistics Wizard [described]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4647
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

