Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Data Source [Chart]
Select from where the Chart gets the data you want to display.
Data Table
For this setting the Chart shows the contents of a DataTable as a diagram.
Type in the name of and path to the data table containing the data, or click the button 
  and select the
table in the dialog Select Object.
Type in the Range of the table cells you want to show.
• To show all cells in all columns and rows, type in {*,*}..{*,*}.
• To show the first four cells of column one, type in {1,1}..{1,4}.
• To show all cells in column one, type in {1,1}..{1,*}.
You can also type in negative numbers:
• To show the one but last column, type in {-2,*}..{-2,*}.
• To show the one but last and the last column of the table, type in {-2,*}..{*,*}.
Input Channels
For this setting the Chart shows the channels contained in the Input Channels table.
Data Source [Chart]
11-4654 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

To open a table into which you type in the input channels, click Input Channels.
These channels are, as a rule, the paths to attributes or methods of objects, whose values you want
to display. You can also type in complex expressions, i.e., method calls, formulas, or the sum of two
attributes. Also type in row and column headers as labels of the Chart.
To delete the entire contents of the input channels table, hold down Shift while you drag-and-drop a new
object onto the Chart.
Note
To specify a formula, type it directly into the respective cell of the DataTable.
Data Source [Chart]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4655
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Do not click the formula button 
  on the List ribbon tab of the DataTable!
Note
To change the order in which the Chart shows the stations, edit the Table of the Input Channels by
cutting the respective columns and pasting them in the desired order.
Note
If the amount of data to be displayed is extremely large, it can take some time to show the Chart. This
applies, for example, to a table containing several tens of thousands of cells. Some chart types, for
example the 3D types, also take a comparatively large amount of time to display.
Worker Pools
For this setting the Chart shows the Workers managed by WorkerPools as a diagram.
• To open a table into which you type in the WorkerPools to be used, click Worker Pools.
Drag the WorkerPools whose Workers you want to show to the cells of the dialog List of Worker Pools
to Configure and click OK.
Data Source [Chart]
