Chart Category
Category [drop-down list]
Select the Category for displaying the data.
Remarks
You can select one of these settings:
• Chart
Shows a number of values or several sets of a number of values.
• Histogram
Shows the frequency distribution for one or several input channels. For this setting you can select the
check box Accumulated.
Note
The input channels for Histograms should to be watchable to show exact values.
• Plotter
Shows the progression of one or more values over time. For this setting you can select the check box
Step Curve.
• 3D Chart
Chart Category
11-4662 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Shows a 3D Chart embedded in the 3D display window with the settings you select. You cannot open
the 3D Chart in a window of its own by clicking Show Chart.
• 3D Histogram
Shows a 3D Histogram embedded in the 3D display window with the settings you select. You cannot
open the 3D Histogram in a window of its own by clicking Show Chart.
• XY Graph
Shows a number of x-y pairs of values or several sets of x-y pairs of values. This setting is only active if
you select Table File as the Data Source.
The XY Graph shows the range like this:
◦ The x values are contained in the first row or column.
◦ The range determines the y values. The first row or column, which contains the x values, will
automatically be excluded.
Note
If you select another Category, the Chart in 3D automatically shows the graphic of this category in the
Frame.
