Category - 3D Chart
The Category 3D Chart shows a 3D Chart embedded in the 3D display window with the settings you
select.
Remarks
Note
You cannot open the 3D Chart in a window of its own by clicking Show Chart.
The category 3D Chart has these properties:
• It has a fixed Font Size. Only the setting Bold affects it. For a Width and/or Height greater than 5
meters, the font size is absolutely fixed. For a size smaller than 5 meters the font size scales down with
all other display elements.
• It uses the settings for the Color and the Line Weight, which you select on the Tab Color, for the setting
Chart Type > Line. It does neither use a Marker Type nor a Line Style.
• It enables you to hide the Base plate and the background of the displayed data by setting the Opacity
of the Background and the Desk to 0 on the Tab Color. This way you can create a transparent chart
which you can lay on top of other graphics or objects.
• Its Base plate has a thickness of 20 cm by default. If you set the Opacity of the Background to 0, it has
a thickness of 10 cm. For a Width and/or Height smaller than 5 meters, the thickness scales down with
all other display elements. If the minimum size is 2.5 m for example, the chart with a base plate has a
thickness of 10 cm and a thickness of 5 cm without a base plate.
A 3D Chart attached to the wall of your factory might look like this.
Category - 3D Chart
Plant Simulation Help 11-4665
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

See also
