Grid Lines X-Axis
To show Grid Lines on the X-Axis in the display window of the Chart, select this check box. To hide them,
clear the check box.
Type in the maximum Number of grid lines that the Chart shows on the x-axis.
SimTalk
YGrid [SimTalk]
XGrid [SimTalk]
XGridlines [SimTalk]
Number
Type in the Number of grid lines which the Chart shows on the x-axis. The Chart also shows a label for
each grid line on the x-axis. If you are displaying a large number of data sets, it makes sense to enter a
smaller number so that the labels can be shown completely.
If the number of grid lines is greater than the number of data sets on the x-axis, the Chart only shows as
many grid lines as there are data sets.
If the number of grid lines is less than the number of data sets, the Chart reduces the number of grid lines
and labels.
Note
For the Category > XY-Graph, the Chart only evaluates the Number, if you also type a fixed Range X,
i.e., if you did not type in an asterisk *.
