Range Y
Type in the first value of the Range the Chart is to display on the y-axis into the left text box.
Remarks
The default setting 0 ... * means that Plant Simulation shows the vales between 0 and the largest
displayed value.
Note
When you activate Logarithmic Y-Axis, you also have to type in a value greater than 0, for example 0.1,
for the Range Y, so that Plant Simulation can display the scale logarithmically.
Type in the last value of the range the Chart is to display scaled on the y-axis into the right text box.
Use the asterisk * to designate open or semi-open ranges along the y-axis and along the x-axis.
Compare these examples:
Type in To do this
* … * Show the values between the smallest and the greatest
displayed value on the y-axis.
0 … * Show the values between 0 and the greatest displayed value
on the y-axis.
* … 7.5 Show the values between the smallest displayed value and
7.5 on the y-axis.
-20 … 20 Show the values between -20 and +20 on the y-axis.
Note
If you specify neither Title nor Subtitle, the Chart might, under certain circumstances, cut off the upper
part of the Range Y.
Type a blank space into the text box Subtitle to prevent this.
SimTalk
YScaleMin [SimTalk]
Range Y
