Range X
Type in the first value of the Range, which the Chart is to display scaled on the x-axis in the left text box.
Remarks
Type the last value of the Range, which the Chart is to display scaled on the x-axis into the right text box.
The default setting 0 … 0 means that Plant Simulation shows the entire range of definition.
If you are only displaying part of the range, the Chart shows a horizontal scrollbar, allowing you to scroll
through the entire range of definition.
For the Category > Histogram, the Range X directly defines the range of definition. Type 0 into the right
text box, so that the Chart dynamically adjusts the upper bound. Type the size of the intervals, into which
the Chart divides the frequency distribution, into the text box Step size.
For the Category > Plotter, the Range X defines the time span, which the Chart shows in the display. You
can also define the Feed Rate by which the Chart scrolls when it reaches the right-hand side of the display.
Type in a number between 0.1 and 12. The number 0.1 stands for smooth scrolling, while 12 scrolls the
entire page.
Use the asterisk * to designate open or semi-open ranges along the x-axis. You can also use it to designate
dynamic upper limits for the Histogram.
Compare these examples:
Type in To do this
* … * Show the values between the smallest and the greatest
displayed value.
0 … * Show the values between 0 and the greatest displayed value
on the x-axis.
* … 7.5 Show the values between the smallest displayed value and
7.5 on the x-axis.
-20 … 20 Show the values between -20 and +20 on the x-axis.
Negative values and 0 are useful for charts of category XY Graph.
SimTalk
XScaleMin [SimTalk]
Range X
