Color [Chart]
The Chart shows the number of the color or the name of item for which you define the color in the column
Color.
Remarks
The tab shows these values:
• Grid (number -3)
Is the color the Chart uses for displaying the grid, i.e., the bounding rectangles, and the grid lines of the
graph proper in the Chart window.
• Background (number -2)
Is the color the Chart uses for displaying the background of the graph proper in the Chart window.
• Desk (number -1)
Is the color the Chart uses for displaying the area located outside of the bounding rectangle of the
graph’s grid in the Chart window.
• Text (number 0)
Is the color the Chart uses for displaying text.
• Colors (numbers 1 through 14)
1 through 14 are the predefined colors of the input channels of the displayed data.
You can add 
  additional colors and define their properties to meet your modeling needs.
Double-click the Color box to open the MS Windows dialog Colors where you define colors.
You can select one of the predefined colors, or you can click More Colors and click the Select button to
select a color in the color matrix. Then click OK. Plant Simulation shows this color next to More Colors and
uses it as the active color.
Color [Chart]
